│                                    ┌ Flash it: the router restarts, and the internet and Wi-Fi are off for a few minut┐                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
│                                    │ This writes the new firmware to the router and restarts it.                      │                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
│                                    │ What happens: owut checks the downloaded image once more, then the router closes │                                    │
│                                    │ every connection, writes the new firmware to its storage and starts again on it. │                                    │
│                                    │ sentry waits and then checks that everything is back.                            │                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
│                                    │ How long: usually 3 to 5 minutes. During that time there is no internet and no   │                                    │
│                                    │ Wi-Fi for any device on this network, this machine included. sentry waits up to  │                                    │
│                                    │ 15 minutes before it says the router hasn't come back.                           │                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
│                                    │ What is kept: all of the router's settings (network, Wi-Fi, firewall, passwords, │                                    │
│                                    │ its ssh keys) and every package installed now; an encrypted backup of the        │                                    │
│                                    │ settings was made by this run before anything was downloaded.                    │                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
│                                    │ What can't be helped from here: if the flash itself fails, nothing automatic can │                                    │
│                                    │ rescue the router; it is then brought back by the device's own recovery          │                                    │
│                                    │ procedure (on its OpenWrt page). Have those instructions at hand, on paper or    │                                    │
│                                    │ another device, before you go on.                                                │                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
│                                    │ Never turn the router off while it is flashing.                                  │                                    │
│                                    │                                                                                  │                                    │
